# corpus-guard allowlist
#
# The corpus guard fails when a blob that existed in the base commit has disappeared.
# A reorganisation is allowed; a disappearance is not. This file is the ONLY way to
# remove a work on purpose: list its blob SHA (the 40-character object name from
# `git ls-tree -r <commit>`), one per line. Removing a line here is itself a
# deliberate act, and it is visible in the pull request that changes this file.
#
# Nothing is on this list. Nothing has been removed.
